.SH "NAME"
econf\&.FileCallback \- function type invoked for each candidate configuration file

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
import "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/bindings/go/econf"
.fi
.ft
.sp
.nf
\fBtype FileCallback func(filename string) bool\fR
.fi

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
\fBeconf\&.FileCallback\fR
is the function type accepted by the
\fB\&.\&.\&.WithCallback\fR
read functions
(\fBReadFileWithCallback\fR,
\fBReadConfigWithCallback\fR,
\fBReadDirsHistoryWithCallback\fR; see
\fBeconf_go_ReadFile\fR(3),
\fBeconf_go_ReadConfig\fR(3)
and
\fBeconf_go_ReadDirsHistory\fR(3))\&.

.PP
A value of this type is invoked once per candidate configuration file
while reading, with the absolute path of that file as
\fIfilename\fR\&. Returning
\fItrue\fR
allows parsing of that file to proceed; returning
\fIfalse\fR
aborts the whole read call, which then fails with
\fBeconf\&.ErrParsingCallbackFailed\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_Error\fR(3))\&.

.PP
This mirrors the
\fIcallback\fR/\fIcallback_data\fR
parameters of the underlying C functions (see
\fBeconf_readFileWithCallback\fR(3)
and
\fBeconf_readConfigWithCallback\fR(3)); the Go binding uses a plain closure
instead of a C function pointer plus opaque
\fIvoid *\fR
data, so arbitrary Go state can be captured directly by the closure\&.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
Not applicable; this page documents a function type\&.

.SH "ERRORS"

.PP
Not applicable; this page documents a function type\&.

.SH "EXAMPLE"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 1
.\}
.nf

package main

import (
    "log"
    "strings"

    "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/bindings/go/econf"
)

func main() {
    var seen []string
    checkFile := econf\&.FileCallback(func(filename string) bool {
        seen = append(seen, filename)
        return !strings\&.Contains(filename, "\&.disabled\&.")
    })

    f, err := econf\&.ReadConfigWithCallback(
        "foo", "/usr/lib", "example", "conf", "=", "#", checkFile)
    if err != nil {
        log\&.Fatal(err)
    }
    defer f\&.Close()

    log\&.Println("inspected files:", seen)
}

.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

